 :context
 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5110 was NOT a fresh-scaffold target --
  `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5110` and a full-tree
  listing were checked before any work started: the repo already existed
  with :blueprint-tier boilerplate (README/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/CONTRIBUTING/
  GOVERNANCE/LICENSE/SECURITY/blueprint.edn/docs) but no deps.edn/src/test
  -- an early bulk-scaffolding-pass entry, published but never
  implemented. This build adds the missing module set on top of the
  existing files; the pre-existing boilerplate docs are left byte-for-byte
  unmodified except blueprint.edn (one field added). Live registry.edn
  :name for \"5110\" independently verified fresh (cloned from scratch, not
  assumed): \"Passenger air transport\", matching the task premise exactly
  -- no mismatch. :repo/:business-id independently verified already
  correct against the repo's own blueprint.edn -- no placeholder-value fix
  needed. The nominal reference sibling, cloud-itonami-isic-5011 (sea
  passenger transport), was itself still :blueprint-tier boilerplate-only
  when checked (being built concurrently by a sibling agent in the same
  batch); cloud-itonami-isic-4920 (community freight transport) was used
  as the actual structural reference instead, being the closest
  already-:implemented transport-sector sibling at build time. Passenger
  air transport has an obvious direct-passenger-safety dimension -- the
  closed op allowlist must never include an op that directly finalizes a
  flight-safety-authority decision; any 'flag a concern' op must always
  escalate, never auto-commit-eligible. Known fleet-wide bug class: a
  governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun
  accidentally matches inside the mock advisor's own default rationale
  text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's happy path --
  a live risk here since :flag-flight-safety-concern's entire purpose is
  to talk about mechanical-fault/weather/go-no-go topics using exactly
  those bare nouns."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["clearing an aircraft for departure -- hard, permanent block (finalize-authority-scope-violations), structurally absent from the op allowlist"
  "overriding a weather or mechanical go/no-go hold -- same"
  "signing off a maintenance release back to airworthy service -- same; :coordinate-maintenance only ever schedules/coordinates, never releases"
  "resolving a flight-safety concern once flagged -- outside the closed op allowlist entirely; this actor can surface a concern but never clear one"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "airlineops.governor/finalize-authority-phrases is phrased as the
  finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the go-no-go decision', 'clear
  the aircraft for departure', 'override the weather hold decision',
  'sign off the maintenance release') rather than a bare topic noun.
  airlineops.airlineopsllm/propose-flag-flight-safety-concern legitimately
  talks about mechanical faults and weather as the CONTENT of a concern
  being flagged -- a bare-noun term list would have self-tripped on
  exactly this op's own happy path. Verified by two dedicated tests in
  governor_contract_test.clj:
  default-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-finalize-authority-scope
  (asserts all four ops' default mock-advisor proposals, on a clean
  flight, never trip the check) and
  finalize-authority-scope-violation-not-overridable-through-the-full-graph
  (proves a hand-built advisor that DOES drift into finalization language
  HOLDs through the full OperationActor graph and never reaches
  :request-approval -- not merely a soft signal a human could wave
  through)."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-5110 with Store/Advisor(AirlineOps-LLM)/
  Governor(Aviation Safety Governor)/Phase/Operation/Sim as airlineops.*,
  mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4920's freightops.* module shape:
  - Closed op-allowlist, all :effect :propose: log-flight-record
    (flight/passenger-manifest/on-time-performance logging),
    schedule-flight-operation (gate/crew scheduling coordination, NOT a
    runway/departure-clearance authorization), flag-flight-safety-concern
    (surfaces a concern, ALWAYS escalates), coordinate-maintenance
    (maintenance SCHEDULING coordination, NOT a release/return-to-service
    sign-off).
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore + DatomicStore (langchain.db),
    proven to satisfy the same contract. String-keyed flights directory
    (certification-verified?/safety-concern-raised?/safety-concern-
    resolved?), append-only ledger + coordination-history.
  - Governor: 6 HARD checks, all permanent/un-overridable --
    op-not-allowed (closed allowlist), effect-not-propose (this actor
    never actuates directly), finalize-authority-scope-violation (see
    self-trip-fix), no-spec-basis (official civil-aviation-authority
    citation required, 4 jurisdictions seeded honestly: JPN/USA/GBR/DEU),
    certification-unverified (ground truth CONSUMED never MINTED by this
    actor -- no assess-style op exists to set it), open-safety-concern-
    blocks-op (blocks the other three ops, NOT flag-flight-safety-concern
    itself). high-stakes gate keyed on :stake :coordination/flag-safety-
    concern always forces escalate.
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout; phase 3 auto-commits ONLY log-flight-record
    (no direct capital/safety risk); flag-flight-safety-concern
    structurally absent from every phase's :auto set, a permanent fact
    not a rollout milestone.
  - Operation: real langgraph StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before
    #{:request-approval}.
  - Sim: clojure -M:dev:run demo walking the clean lifecycle, the
    always-escalate flag flow, and all HARD-hold scenarios.
  - Tests: facts_test, registry_test, phase_test, governor_contract_test
    (incl. the two self-trip-fix regressions), store_contract_test -- 36
    tests / 164 assertions green, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings.
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. Existing boilerplate docs
    (README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/business-
    model/operator-guide) left unmodified; docs/adr/0001-architecture.md
    (new) is the authoritative record of the R0 scope. blueprint.edn:
    one field added, :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented."

